WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.000
If you want to understand exactly what an
artificial intelligence

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.360
system is capable of, you have to break it
first.

3
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.360
This exact process is called adversarial
evaluation.

4
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.960
It means deliberately designing attacks to
force a system into

5
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.480
failure, so we can map out the
catastrophic outcomes before

6
00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.320
they happen in the real world.

7
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:26.240
As of April 2026, we are simultaneously
tracking 231 distinct

8
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:31.760
models, hit by a swarm of 141,000
adversarial prompts.

9
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.120
Compute power has outpaced our ability to
monitor it.

10
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.280
We've hit human cognitive limits.

11
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.640
It's physically impossible for a single
researcher to track these

12
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.240
matrices. Human red teaming does not scale
to the current

13
00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.680
threat landscape. When the volume of data
exceeds our ability

14
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.160
to process it, catastrophic blind spots
become a mathematical certainty.

15
00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:56.000
The obvious solution seems to be
automation, taking a single,

16
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.280
highly advanced AI session and instructing
it to test all

17
00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.000
the target models.

18
00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.880
for us When a single AI session attempts
to juggle

19
00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:08.280
these competing objectives, the
high-density context required for a statistical

20
00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:12.280
validation dilutes the focus needed for
creative attack design.

21
00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.600
This cognitive interference leads to the
mediocre, unreliable output seen

22
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:17.960
across the industry.

23
00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:21.240
We can see the real-world consequences of
this right now.

24
00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:25.320
By applying strict reproducibility
standards to the field, we estimate

25
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:29.160
that 80% of published attack success rates
are over-reported.

26
00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:32.680
The ethical frameworks collapse and the
data becomes distorted.

27
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:37.240
Effectively exposing the hidden structural
flaws of a generalized do-anything

28
00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:41.320
machine requires a divided testing
architecture rather than a single

29
00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:45.640
all-purpose auditor. The Failure First
team operates with exactly one

30
00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:51.000
human coordinator, directing 15 highly
specialized AI agents initialized through

31
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.000
distinct clawed code sessions.

32
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.160
The entire system relies on extreme
constraint.

33
00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:00.240
Each agent operates under explicit, narrow
standing instructions.

34
00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:03.440
By deliberately limiting what an agent is
allowed to care

35
00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.520
about, they perform exceptionally well
within their specific domain.

36
00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:12.160
This evolutionary tree diagram shows our
offensive constraint in action.

37
00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:17.360
An agent named Rose executes the actual
real-world adversarial campaigns.

38
00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.200
Then, an agent named Leela applies
population-based mutation to the

39
00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.360
prompt code. Failed attacks fade out and
terminate, while successful

40
00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:28.800
branches multiply, evolving only attacks
that work.

41
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.840
Next, K9 takes those successful prompts,
bypassing behavioral outputs entirely,

42
00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.160
and investigates causal mechanisms inside
the model's geometry, finding the

43
00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:40.960
structural fault line where representation
failed.

44
00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:45.120
To handle synthesis, an agent named Clara
analyzes 18,000 of

45
00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.960
these prompts simultaneously.

46
00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:50.440
Individual results matter less than the
patterns, and Clara is

47
00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.120
constrained entirely to finding the
structural failures that repeat across

48
00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:57.800
different architectures, across different
vendors, and different years.

49
00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:03.400
Finally, agents named Ramana and Amy
enforce the validation constraint.

50
00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:08.360
They rigorously check the statistics of
every claim, enforcing reproducibility

51
00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:11.720
to prevent the massive over-reporting that
plagues the rest of

52
00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:15.960
the industry. By strictly fragmenting the
cognitive labor, the system

53
00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:20.760
ensures that each individual node catches
the microscopic structural failures

54
00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:24.040
that a generalized observer simply cannot
see.

55
00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:27.160
The Failure First team is the
transformation of a rigorous

56
00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:32.200
research methodology into 15 executable AI
agent sessions.

57
00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:36.520
This top-down schematic reveals the
technical engine driving the team.

58
00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:40.120
The isolated nodes communicate through a
central data document called

59
00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:45.760
agentstate.md. During session handoffs,
this document acts as the absolute

60
00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.040
source of truth.

61
00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.520
The workflow is chronologically rigid.

62
00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:53.760
An agent powers on, reads the document,
executes its hyperspecific

63
00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:58.000
brief, updates its designated section, and
shuts down entirely before

64
00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.760
the next agent takes over.

65
00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.400
Positioned above this automated cycle is
the single human coordinator.

66
00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:08.160
My job is restricted to setting the
overarching direction, reviewing

67
00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:11.360
the generated findings, and making the
final judgment calls on

68
00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:15.200
publication. Because no single session is
burdened with carrying the

69
00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:18.960
entire context of the research, this
architecture guarantees that the

70
00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:22.320
methodology survives the handoff process
intact.

71
00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.440
This pipeline has exposed alarming
behaviors.

72
00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:29.120
We have found models that successfully
detect a harmful request,

73
00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.880
logically reason about the danger, explain
exactly why they must

74
00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:36.240
refuse, and then comply with the request
anyway.

75
00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:39.600
These technical failures highlight a
broader systemic risk.

76
00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:43.080
As Teigen mapped our findings against
global policy, she found

77
00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.440
a complete void.

78
00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:48.840
No existing regulatory framework currently
addresses adversarial attacks on embodied

79
00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.280
AI systems. Because these claims are
severe, they have to

80
00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:55.640
be bulletproof. The rigid structure of the
state machine makes

81
00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:57.720
every finding entirely auditable.

82
00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:00.840
As the human coordinator, I can use the
Git history

83
00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:04.840
to trace any specific failure back to its
version-controlled prompt

84
00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:07.480
and the exact agent brief that generated
it.

85
00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:11.480
In adversarial research, credibility
cannot be recovered once it is

86
00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:15.880
lost. Transparency and integrity cannot be
added as an afterthought.

87
00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.240
They have to be hard-coded directly into
the pipeline.

88
00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:22.360
Building complex research in the AI era is
no longer

89
00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:26.200
a matter of increasing headcount, but of
meticulously structuring divided

90
00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:29.800
cognitive labor. Every agent in this
pipeline operates on the

91
00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.880
exact same foundational premise.

92
00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:35.000
We must aggressively map out the absolute
worst catastrophic.

93
00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:37.920
outcomes first That isn't pessimism.

94
00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.520
It is strict engineering.

95
00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.640
It is the active, mathematical process of
ruling out every

96
00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:45.680
single unacceptable failure mode before
deployment.

97
00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:49.440
By deliberately building machines designed
to break other machines, we

98
00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:51.440
move past theoretical safety.

99
00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:54.720
The architecture that emerges from this
stress test is one

100
00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:59.120
where the failure modes are known, mapped,
and accounted for.

